<h1>Reform options: how the yearly increase could change</h1>

<p class="lede">This page compares five rules for the yearly increase, including the one announced for April 2030: how far they differ depends on how prices and earnings move, and where they differ the gap grows over time. Two separate decisions are often discussed together. One is how the State Pension should rise each year. The other is who should be entitled to it. This page sets out the options for the yearly increase, the arguments for and against the triple lock, and what evidence can and cannot settle about them.</p>

